.claude/
# occ's own project-level directory. Blanket-ignored like .claude/ above;
# anything meant to be team-shared (skills/, agents/, settings.json) is
# force-added with `git add -f`, which is how .claude/ is tracked today.
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: occ puts its git worktrees under
# `.occ/worktrees/<name>/`, so a checkout of this repo can itself live at a
# path containing a `.occ` segment. knip matches gitignore patterns against
# absolute paths, so an unanchored `.occ/` also matches that ancestor segment
# and silently drops the entry points it discovers by expanding package.json
# `exports` globs — `bun run check:unused` then reports all ~77 files under
# packages/builtin-tools/src/tools/ as unused. Anchoring keeps the intent
# (ignore the repo-root .occ directory) without matching ancestors.
/.occ/
.omx/
.docs/task/
# Binary / screenshot files (root only)
/*.png
*.bmp

# Internal system prompt documents
Claude-Opus-*.txt
Claude-Sonnet-*.txt
Claude-Haiku-*.txt

